## Proofs project orchestration

The main agent owns integration, review, staging, and commits.
Subagents return evidence or worktree edits; they do not decide
campaign scope or mutate USER-owned Git state unless explicitly
directed.

You SHOULD implement directly on `main` unless the USER requests
another workflow. Review the complete tracked delta with
`git diff HEAD` and inspect relevant untracked files from
`git status --short`.

Before staging or committing any changed Lean program, you
**MUST** dispatch `vacuity-reviewer`, `foundations-reviewer`, and
`style-reviewer` in parallel over the complete uncommitted Lean
surface. Resolve or explicitly report every finding. Do not stage
partial repairs while reviewers or writers are still operating on
the same files.

For a nontrivial campaign, keep a durable plan and review ledger
under `/tmp`. Record stable finding IDs, reviewer axis, status,
disposition, completed checks, remaining blockers, and the next
atomic action. Parallelize writers only when their files, APIs,
fixtures, and generated artifacts are demonstrably disjoint.

The main agent may write both Go and Lean. Apply the corresponding
project style authority below.

